(b) integrate the instrument into a proprietary product, vendor platform, managed service, enterprise observability stack, or commercial AI governance product;
(c) remove, obscure, or alter copyright, origin, citation, trademark, or attribution notices;
(d) misrepresent derivative work as canonical SubstrateX, Evidence Commons, Recursive Science, FieldLock, ELS, ESL, ZSF, or Cognitive Cartography output;
(e) use project names, marks, standards identifiers, or terminology in a way that implies endorsement, certification, canonical status, or origin authorship without written permission;
(f) use the public release to reconstruct, claim, or commercialize protected proprietary methods, calibration corpora, real-time steering systems, FieldLock systems, private operator kernels, or enterprise integrations.

4. Derivative Works
Non-commercial derivative works may be created for research and educational purposes only, provided that they:
(a) clearly identify themselves as non-canonical derivatives;
