(d) do not claim ELS/ESL/ZSF conformance if semantics materially diverge from the published specifications.

5. Evidence and Standards Semantics
Terms including Basin Exit, Observable Failure, Lead-Time, ESL, ELS, ZSF, Evidence Commons, Runtime Evidence, Cognitive Cartography, Chronodynamics, and FieldLock carry specific origin and standards meanings. Modified systems must explicitly label divergence and may not create standards drift by using canonical terminology with materially altered semantics.

